<title>URUGUAY: SOCCER-URUGUAY BEAT BOLIVIA 1-0 IN WORLD CUP QUALIFIER.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-URUGUAY BEAT BOLIVIA 1-0 IN WORLD CUP QUALIFIER.</headline>
<dateline>MONTEVIDEO 1996-10-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Uruguay beat Bolivia 1-0</p>
<p>(halftime 0-0) in a South American World Cup qualifying match</p>
<p>on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Scorer: Juan Manuel Pena, own goal (62nd minute)</p>
<p>Attendance: 70,000</p>
<p>Standings (tabuluate under played, won, drawn, lost, goals</p>
<p>for, goals against, points):</p>
<p> Colombia    4  3  1  0  9  3 10</p>
<p> Ecuador     4  3  0  1  8  5  9</p>
<p> Uruguay     4  2  0  2  4  5  6</p>
<p> Argentina   4  1  2  1  4  4  5</p>
<p> Bolivia     4  1  1  2  7  5  4</p>
<p> Chile	 3  1  1  1  6  6  4</p>
<p> Paraguay    3  1  1  1  3  2  4</p>
<p> Peru	  4  0  3  1  2  5  3</p>
<p> Venezuela   4  0  1  3  2 10  1</p>
<p>Playing Wednesday: Ecuador v Colombia, Paraguay v Chile,</p>
<p>Venezuela v Argentina</p>
<p>Note: top four teams qualify for the 1998 World Cup in</p>
<p>France. Brazil qualify automatically as holders.</p>
</text>
